\ Self-recursive tail call with a symbolic row beneath it. A runtime-depth
\ `drop-at` collapses the stack into an opaque row before the recursive call, so
\ the tail call cannot use the loop-back-edge argument copy and is emitted as an
\ ordinary recursive call against the live stack. Built under runtime-image AOT,
\ so the result comes from the compiled path and matches the interpreter.

\ Sum 1..n with an accumulator. Each non-base step pushes a throwaway sentinel
\ and removes it with a runtime-depth `drop-at`, collapsing the live stack into a
\ row, then performs the tail-recursive call against that row.
row-sum: ( n acc -- total ) [
  over 0 = [
    nip
  ] [
    over + swap 1 - swap
    \ stack: (n-1) (acc+n) ; push sentinel, drop it at runtime depth 0 -> row
    777 0 drop-at
    row-sum
  ] if
] ;

5 0 row-sum . "--" print-line
0 0 row-sum . "--" print-line
1 0 row-sum . "--" print-line
